# Root-level npm scaffolding, not project code. Agent tooling (e.g.
# `npm i @anthropic-ai/claude-agent-sdk`) run from the repo root leaves a
# package.json/package-lock.json here that belongs to nothing in the build.
#
# ROOT-ANCHORED ON PURPOSE. There are a dozen tracked package.json /
# package-lock.json files under docs/, elixir/web-ng/assets/, js/cli/ and
# js/create-dashboard/, and one of them is a declared Bazel input
# (npm_translate_lock resolves @web_ng_npm from it -- see the pnpm-lock note
# below). An unanchored `package.json` would match every one of those. The
# leading slash keeps this to the repo root only.
/package.json
/package-lock.json

